WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.742
DATE is appropriate when the calendar day matters but the time of day does not.

00:00:04.742 --> 00:00:08.282
Examples include birth date or a reporting date.

00:00:08.282 --> 00:00:13.147
A typed date can be sorted chronologically and used in date arithmetic.

00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:18.807
A text string that merely looks like a date does not provide the same analytical guarantees.

00:00:18.807 --> 00:00:21.732
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:21.732 --> 00:00:25.087
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:25.087 --> 00:00:29.502
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:35.757
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:37.452
daylight-saving changes.
